From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 21:12:01 +0000
Subject: Do not arm the lock timer after the screensaver in a Unity session

In a Unity session Unity asks for the blank (SetActive) when the session
goes idle and decides itself whether and when to lock, from
org.gnome.desktop.screensaver lock-enabled and lock-delay. The timer that
locks lock-after-screensaver seconds after the blank would lock regardless
of those settings, so it is not armed when XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP lists Unity.
The lock-after-screensaver setting itself is not changed: light-locker
writes its settings back at start, so a different default would not take
effect for existing users and would carry over to other desktops.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-13
